      "ownershipVehicle": "Argo Infrastructure Partners",
      "description": "Oneta Energy Center is a natural gas-fired combined-cycle power plant in Broken Arrow, Wagoner County, Oklahoma, operated by Oneta Power, LLC. The single-plant business sells electricity and capacity into wholesale markets in the Southwest Power Pool. Its official site describes approximately 1,150 MW of nominal capacity, LS Power's 2019 sale announcement described 1,127 MW, and a FERC asset appendix attributes 1,086 MW for market-based-rate reporting. LS Power announced an agreement to sell Oneta and Carville to an Argo-managed investment vehicle on August 15, 2019; FERC reports a November 21, 2019 control-transfer date. EPA's 2023 facility record identifies Argo Infrastructure Partners LP as the 100% parent. Oneta Power and Oneta Energy Center are the operator and facility identities for one Argo investment, not separate manager-level portfolio companies. No later sale or signed pending ownership transfer was identified through August 16, 2026.",
